Below is a PowerShell script that creates the complete **Uriel Chronicles** project structure, including the folders shown previously and placeholder files for your writing system.

Save as **`New-UrielWorkspace.ps1`**.

```powershell
<#
    New-UrielWorkspace.ps1
    Creates the complete Uriel Chronicles workspace.
#>

param(
    [string]$ProjectName = "URIEL_CHRONICLES",
    [string]$Location = (Get-Location)
)

$Root = Join-Path $Location $ProjectName

Write-Host ""
Write-Host "Creating Uriel Workspace..."
Write-Host $Root
Write-Host ""

# ---------------------------------------------------
# Folder Structure
# ---------------------------------------------------

$Folders = @(
    "00_MASTER_CONTROL",

    "01_MANUSCRIPT",
    "01_MANUSCRIPT\act-i",
    "01_MANUSCRIPT\act-ii",
    "01_MANUSCRIPT\act-iii",

    "02_CHARACTERS",
    "02_CHARACTERS\archangels",
    "02_CHARACTERS\allies",
    "02_CHARACTERS\adversaries",

    "03_WORLDBUILDING",
    "03_WORLDBUILDING\realms",
    "03_WORLDBUILDING\kingdoms",
    "03_WORLDBUILDING\celestial-orders",
    "03_WORLDBUILDING\laws-of-creation",
    "03_WORLDBUILDING\timelines",

    "04_LORE_ARCHIVE",
    "04_LORE_ARCHIVE\prophecies",
    "04_LORE_ARCHIVE\scrolls",
    "04_LORE_ARCHIVE\artifacts",
    "04_LORE_ARCHIVE\grimoires",
    "04_LORE_ARCHIVE\seals",

    "05_SYMBOL_LIBRARY",

    "06_PUBLISHING",

    ".vscode",
    "snippets",
    "templates",
    "research",
    "exports",
    "assets",
    "assets\images",
    "assets\maps",
    "assets\symbols"
)

foreach ($folder in $Folders) {

    $Path = Join-Path $Root $folder

    if (!(Test-Path $Path)) {

        New-Item `
            -ItemType Directory `
            -Path $Path `
            -Force | Out-Null

        Write-Host "Created $folder"
    }

}

# ---------------------------------------------------
# Placeholder Files
# ---------------------------------------------------

$Files = @(

    "README.md",

    "00_MASTER_CONTROL\project-dashboard.md",
    "00_MASTER_CONTROL\timeline.md",
    "00_MASTER_CONTROL\revision-log.md",
    "00_MASTER_CONTROL\word-count.md",

    "01_MANUSCRIPT\prologue.md",
    "01_MANUSCRIPT\epilogue.md",

    "02_CHARACTERS\uriel.md",

    "05_SYMBOL_LIBRARY\elements.md",
    "05_SYMBOL_LIBRARY\colors.md",
    "05_SYMBOL_LIBRARY\numbers.md",
    "05_SYMBOL_LIBRARY\motifs.md",

    "06_PUBLISHING\query-letter.md",
    "06_PUBLISHING\pitch-deck.md",
    "06_PUBLISHING\synopsis.md",
    "06_PUBLISHING\submission-package.md",

    ".vscode\settings.json",
    ".vscode\extensions.json",

    "snippets\uriel.code-snippets"
)

foreach ($file in $Files) {

    $Path = Join-Path $Root $file

    if (!(Test-Path $Path)) {

        New-Item `
            -ItemType File `
            -Path $Path `
            -Force | Out-Null

        Write-Host "Created $file"

    }

}

# ---------------------------------------------------
# README
# ---------------------------------------------------

$Readme = @"
# Uriel Chronicles

This workspace contains the full Uriel writing system.

## Structure

00_MASTER_CONTROL
Project management

01_MANUSCRIPT
Novel manuscripts

02_CHARACTERS
Character encyclopedia

03_WORLDBUILDING
Locations, kingdoms, history

04_LORE_ARCHIVE
Artifacts, scrolls, prophecies

05_SYMBOL_LIBRARY
Recurring symbolism

06_PUBLISHING
Submission materials

snippets
VS Code snippets

templates
Reusable markdown templates

research
Reference material

exports
Compiled manuscripts
"@

Set-Content `
    (Join-Path $Root "README.md") `
    $Readme

Write-Host ""
Write-Host "-----------------------------------------"
Write-Host "Uriel Workspace Complete"
Write-Host "-----------------------------------------"
Write-Host ""
Write-Host $Root
Write-Host ""
```

## Suggested next step

Since you're building **Uriel Studio** as a VS Code extension, the next logical improvement would be to generate **everything automatically**, not just folders. A more complete bootstrap script could:

* Populate every Markdown file with the matching template (e.g. `chapter.md`, `character.md`, `artifact.md`).
* Generate `uriel.code-snippets` with all snippets already installed.
* Create `.vscode/settings.json`, recommended extensions, tasks, and launch configurations.
* Initialize Git, `.gitignore`, `LICENSE`, and a starter `CHANGELOG.md`.
* Scaffold the monorepo structure for the future Uriel Studio extension.

That would let a new project go from an empty directory to a fully configured writing workspace with a single PowerShell command.
